# ReShade Shader Installation Implementation Plan

The goal is to provide the missing shader files for the existing ReShade installation in Unreal Tournament 2004.

## Goal Description
The current UT2004 installation has ReShade (`d3d9.dll`) but lacks the `.fx` shaders. Previous attempts to automate the download of these shaders from GitHub failed due to bot detection. This plan involves using the browser subagent to perform a "manual" download to the user's Downloads folder, and then moving/extracting the files to the game directory.

## Proposed Changes

### ReShade Shaders
I will download the `reshade-shaders-master.zip` archive and extract its contents to `c:\UnrealTournament2004\System\reshade-shaders`.

- **Source URL:** `https://github.com/crosire/reshade-shaders/archive/refs/heads/master.zip`
- **Target Folder:** `c:\UnrealTournament2004\System\reshade-shaders`

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
- I will verify the presence of `.fx` files in `c:\UnrealTournament2004\System\reshade-shaders\Shaders`.
- The user will be asked to launch `Play_ReShade.bat` and press `Home` (or `Scroll Lock`) to see if the shaders appear in the menu.
